// Shutter Polarity Concept
// Each gate has two shutters:
//   Active/Day shutter  → force moving outward (projection, expression, external effect)
//   Passive/Night shutter → force moving inward (reception, internalization, reflection)
//
// The same spirit/current appears differently depending on:
//   - which shutter is open
//   - which side of the gate the operator is standing on
// One configuration is for when the force is moving outward;
// the other is for when it is moving inward.
// Names and exact rankings are not fixed forever (sources disagree);
// the structure is directional and polar.

